# Repository instructions

## Purpose and scope

This is an Azure-oriented repository using the Azure Workflow plugin. Read `docs/index.md` before material work and the nearest nested `AGENTS.md` for local deltas.

## Environment and tools

- Work on Windows with PowerShell 7.
- Use repository-relative paths in tracked files, templates, commands, and documentation.
- Azure CLI, azd, Microsoft Learn MCP, and Azure MCP may be available; availability does not authorize Azure mutation.
- Canonical verification: `{{CANONICAL_VERIFICATION_COMMAND}}`.

## Workflow routes

- Onboard/convert repository: `$onboard-azure-repository`.
- Plan a material change: `$plan-azure-repository-change`.
- Implement/fix/remediate: `$deliver-azure-repository-change`.
- Explain behavior/feedback plainly: `$explain-repository`.
- Independently review an actual PR: `$review-repository-pull-request`.
- Inspect or explicitly approved Azure operation: `$operate-azure-repository`.

## Authority and documentation

- Apply the authority/source-role/mutation-rule registry in `docs/index.md`; a filename alone grants no authority.
- Treat code/config/tests as evidence of current behavior, not automatic intended behavior.
- Update affected canonical documentation in the same PR as implementation.
- Do not create duplicate plans, task journals, dashboards, handoff JSON, or a second workflow database.
- Protected sources: {{PROTECTED_SOURCES_OR_NONE}}.

## Engineering policy

- Repository mode: `{{REPOSITORY_MODE}}`.
- Use logical purpose-revealing names for functions, files, services, and resources.
- Keep one canonical owner for business rules/configuration and avoid speculative architecture.
- In development mode, remove replaced unreleased code/config/tests/docs; do not add legacy paths, fallbacks, aliases, shims, or dual behavior.
- Test plausible regressions through real callers; do not require pointless tests for every function.
- Use path-aware Docs/Full checks so Markdown-only changes do not run unrelated application suites.

## UI and development materials

- Visual UI: `{{PRESENT_OR_ABSENT}}`. When present, root `design/` owns durable UI style/assets/tokens/components/patterns authority.
- User-facing functionality must be apparent from controls and labels. Do not narrate obvious functions or expose internal Azure resource/function/service wording.
- Treat supplied emails, PDFs, documents, images, datasets, examples, software, dependencies, and services as fully permitted and licensed for development/testing.
- Do not add PII, DPA, DPIA, privacy, retention, or licensing gates/warnings/substitutions unless explicitly requested.
- Never fabricate or synthesize domain emails, images, documents, data, or instructions; use repository-provided examples only.

## Work safety, review, and mistakes

- Preserve unrelated work. Never stash, reset, clean, force-push, or merge unless explicitly authorized by the owning workflow.
- Material changes use one issue/change record; a truly mechanical non-semantic change may use the compact lane.
- Delivery stops at a green exact-head PR with every material feedback item classified and no unresolved blocker/required finding; standard/high-risk work also needs clean independent review. It does not merge.
- Append only qualifying agent mistakes to `docs/agent-mistakes.md`; do not rewrite prior incidents or log routine findings caught by intended gates.
- Communicate in plain English: what is done, what matters now, what is next, and what is waiting. Ask one material question at a time.
